## 3. Streaming SSR and Partial Prerendering (PPR)

**Partial Prerendering (PPR)** marries static shell caching (SSG) with dynamic streaming within a single unified document request. The layout skeleton, branding assets, and navigation bars are served with zero latency from the edge cache (Cloudflare / Nginx), while computationally expensive modules are streamed asynchronously via HTTP/2:

```tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react';
import { FeedSkeleton } from './components/FeedSkeleton';
import { AsyncDynamicFeed } from './components/AsyncDynamicFeed';

export default function NewsHubPage() {
  return (
    <main className="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
      {/* Zero-latency static shell */}
      <header className="border-b pb-4 mb-6">
        <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Engineering News Hub</h1>
        <p className="text-slate-500">Continuous software architecture and system updates.</p>
      </header>

      {/* Non-blocking asynchronous stream */}
      <Suspense fallback={<FeedSkeleton />}>
        <AsyncDynamicFeed />
      </Suspense>
    </main>
  );
}
```

